   I think this property of humans is more or less builtin to our
brains and how they work. It would be better called `confidence factor'
Imagine if the brain was a neural network and neuron's stored real numbers
in the interval [0,1] Now imagine you were looking at an area
being trained to recognize crows. The neurons in this area might
bounce around wildly, but each time the person sees a black crow, the
the value will be pushed towards a stable equilibrium forcing the person
to believe with high confidence that the next crow he will see is black.

